==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1432. From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|topographye}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|topographia}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|τοπογραφία|}}, from {{m|grc|τόπος||place}} + {{m|grc|γράφω||I write}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/təˈpɒɡɹəfi/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/təˈpɑɡɹəfi/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|top|og|raphy|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|topographies}}

# a [[precise]] [[description]] of a [[place]]
# a [[detail]]ed [[graphic]] [[representation]] of the [[surface]] [[feature]]s of a place or [[object]]
# the features themselves (the [[terrain]])
# the [[surveying]] of the features

